
## Project
EduFlow — plataforma SaaS de gestão educacional para alunos, professores e gestores.

## Stack
React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui,
TanStack Query v5, Supabase (Auth + Postgres + Storage + Edge Functions), Vitest

## Commands
- Dev:         `npm run dev`
- Build:       `npm run build`
- Test single: `npm run test -- src/test/example.test.ts`
- Test all:    `npm run test`
- Lint:        `npm run lint`

- Type check:  `npm run build` (tsc via vite build)

## Architecture
- `src/hooks/`              → domain hooks (useProfile, useTeacherData, etc.)
- `src/components/teacher/` → TeacherClasses, ClassCard, CreateClassModal
- `src/components/student/` → student panel components
- `src/components/manager/` → manager panel components
- `src/pages/`              → one page per role dashboard + auth pages
- `src/contexts/`           → AuthContext (auth state + role detection)
- `src/types/index.ts`      → all shared domain types
- `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` → Supabase client instance
- `supabase/functions/`     → Edge Functions (Deno runtime)
- `supabase/setup/supabase.sql` → full idempotent schema (v3.3)
- `src/hooks/useDashboardData.ts` → barrel re-export only, do not add logic here

## Rules
- Never import from `useDashboardData.ts` in new code — use domain hooks directly
- Always wrap hooks with `() =>` — never call useQuery/useMutation at module level
- All mutations must call `queryClient.invalidateQueries` for affected query keys
- RLS is enabled on all tables — never use service role key on the frontend
- `ispresent` column in attendance is soft-deprecated — always use `status` instead
- Student document URLs are storage paths, not public URLs — always use signed URLs
- `studentCpf` in create-asaas-charge is hardcoded — do not use in production as-is
- IMPORTANT: never modify `supabase/setup/supabase.sql` without running it on a test db first

## Workflow
- Write plan to `tasks/todo.md` before touching any file
- One concern per commit — never mix refactor + feature + fix in the same commit
- Commit format: `feat:` `fix:` `refactor:` `docs:` `chore:`
- Tests required for any new hook or utility function
- Ask before: changing RLS policies, modifying DB schema, touching auth flow
- Act without asking: bug fixes, adding JSDoc, refactoring within existing patterns

## Out of scope
- `src/components/ui/` → shadcn/ui primitives, do not modify
- `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` → auto-generated, do not edit manually
- `supabase/functions/create-asaas-charge/` → payment logic, ask before touching
- `.env` and `.env.local` files → never read or modify